{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And you shall make for yourselves a carved image of the likeness of anything that YHWH your Elohim has commanded you.</b> By way of the plain sense (peshat): the likeness of anything that YHWH your Elohim commanded you — not to make; or it warns concerning the fashioning of the cherubim, which are a forbidden thing, that they should not be made on earth but only in the Temple — and this is 'that YHWH your Elohim commanded you,' to make them in the Temple." "<b>And by way of</b> the Kabbalah: 'that YHWH your Elohim commanded you' — this is the Glory of YHWH, the consuming fire at the top of the mountain, in which Moses sinned and angered Him in the matter of the Rock; therefore he mentioned here, 'and YHWH was angry with me for your sakes,' to prevent me from crossing over — by the authority of the verse, 'Take heed to yourselves, lest you forget the covenant of YHWH your Elohim' — the consuming fire at the top of the mountain — 'and you make for yourselves a carved image of the likeness of anything that YHWH your Elohim has commanded you.' And the verse comes according to its plain sense and meaning: 'for YHWH your Elohim is a consuming fire' — He is the attribute of judgment; and you have already seen this at Sinai, 'a fire consuming at the top of the mountain,' and if you do so, He is an El who is zealous, jealous over idolaters. And what He added, the word הוא, is because הוא is the name of the Holy One, blessed be He, in the manner of what is written (Numbers 18) ״ועבד הלוי הוא״, and it is written (Psalms 100) ״הוא עשנו ולו אנחנו״, and the father of them all (Isaiah 42) ״אני ה׳ הוא שמי״; therefore He needed to add הוא, that is, His name and not His essence — for as to His essence itself, the verse says (Exodus 33) ״כי לא יראני האדם וחי״, for the name of a thing is not the thing itself in truth. And the matter is according to its plain sense: that He means to say, 'a consuming fire, a fire consuming,' for against idolaters His jealousy will burn them like fire. And the fire-worshipers who bring proof from this verse that the Creator is fire — Elijah refutes them, as he said (I Kings 19) ״לא באש ה׳״. And here too their refutation is sound, from what He added and said, 'an El who is jealous,' which explains that what He called 'a consuming fire' is but a metaphor, and the metaphor refers only to the matter of jealousy."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:45:27.606805730Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}